// =============================================================================
//  client.hml — INPUT -> COMMAND -> WIRE, and PACKET -> PICTURE.       W4-11.
// =============================================================================
//
//  The client half of ARCHITECTURE §3. It owns four things and nothing else:
//
//      1. the CAMERA          (`src/render/view.hml` — aim is client-authored)
//      2. the COMMAND         (input latched, quantised, sequenced, sent)
//      3. the RENDER SNAPSHOT (the packet decoded, then interpolated by alpha)
//      4. the EVENT LOG       (the owner block's cosmetic queue turned into
//                              sounds, particles and HUD state)
//
//  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  IT CANNOT READ `world.*`, AND THAT IS STRUCTURAL
//  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  This file does not import `src/sim/world.hml`. It never sees a `World`. It
//  is handed exactly two things per tick — the snapshot PACKET and the OWNER
//  BLOCK — and it decodes the first with `snapshot_read`, which is the same
//  decoder a v2 client runs on bytes off a socket. `rsnap_build_from_net` then
//  turns the decoded frame into the RenderSnapshot. Both calls already existed;
//  W4-11 only had to refuse the shortcut.
//
//  BUILD_PLAN W4-11's acceptance criterion "the renderer never reads world.*"
//  is therefore not a grep result that happens to be clean — there is no code
//  path from here to a world field.
//
//  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  WHAT IS PREDICTED IN v1, AND WHAT IS NOT.  READ THIS BEFORE ADDING LATENCY.
//  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  ARCHITECTURE §3 writes the v1 client as "read back", v2 as "predict +
//  reconcile", and this file is honest about being v1:
//
//    PREDICTED (instant, never waits for the server, never reconciled):
//      * AIM. Mouse-look is client-authored — `view_aim_*` IS the number that
//        goes into the command, and `view_render_*` (aim + recoil kick) is the
//        number that goes into the MVP. Neither ever waits for a packet. This
//        is the single reason 120 ms of fake latency is playable at all.
//      * EVERY COSMETIC OF FIRING. The muzzle flash, the viewmodel kick, the
//        shot sound, the tracer, the screen shake and the dry-fire click all
//        fire on the INPUT FRAME, from `client_press_fire`, with no server
//        round trip. NETWORKING's rule and BUILD_PLAN's criterion:
//        "NS_FAKE_LATENCY_MS=250 still fires the weapon on frame 0 with full
//        cosmetic feedback."
//      * The FOV lerp, the shake envelope, the kick decay, the HUD timers, the
//        particle pool. All frame-time, all client-only, none replicated.
//
//    NOT PREDICTED (authoritative, arrives when it arrives):
//      * POSITION. The body moves when the server says it moved.
//      * DAMAGE, DEATH, AMMO, XP. Everything with a number in it.
//
//  The consequence is exact and it is the right trade for v1: there is no
//  reconciliation, therefore there is no rubber-banding — not "we tuned it
//  out", but "the code that could produce it does not exist". The cost is that
//  translation lags by the one-way delay. `PredictedState`,
//  `predicted_capture`/`predicted_restore` and the owner block are all already
//  shaped for the v2 version; what is missing is a replay of unacknowledged
//  commands, and that is a v2 task with a v2 test.
//
//  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  ART AND AUDIO ARRIVE AS NUMBERS (ARCHITECTURE §5.6b, applied one layer up)
//  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  This file names no atlas cell and no sound file. It emits SEMANTIC ids —
//  `CFX_*` for a particle's look, `CSND_*` for a sound's meaning — and
//  `main.hml` binds them to `fxgen` cells and `audiobank` sfx with
//  `client_bind_fx_cells` / by mapping `CSND_*`. That is what keeps this file
//  linkable with no SDL: `tools/probe_game.hml` builds it headless and asserts
//  `nm | grep -c SDL_ == 0`.
// =============================================================================

